# Hold, Then Drag (#178, PR #292; docs/steps/2026-11-19-ready-292.md) on the agents' Duo (iOS 27.1): the Settings panel
# at its switch, at its default (on since Noah's 2026-11-20, no argument) and turned off, sideways, and on by name
# upright and in large type; the tour's picture card at the default (the drag in the hold's row) and with the switch
# off (main's words: it must be main's pixel for pixel); and the stream screen at the default, which must be main's
# (the switch draws nothing there). Main ignores -Sill.holdThenDrag and -SillSettingsScroll holddrag (its panel then
# opens at the top).
#   Scripts/harness-photos.sh Scripts/harness-photos/hold-then-drag-duo.cases --baseline origin/main
duo-holddrag-off        -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillSettings 1 -SillSettingsScroll holddrag -Sill.holdThenDrag 0
duo-holddrag-on         -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillSettings 1 -SillSettingsScroll holddrag
duo-holddrag-upright    -SillLayout 669x951 -SillHinge flat -SillSettings 1 -SillSettingsScroll holddrag -Sill.holdThenDrag 1
duo-holddrag-ax         -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillSettings 1 -SillSettingsScroll holddrag -Sill.holdThenDrag 1 -UIPreferredContentSizeCategoryName UICTContentSizeCategoryAccessibilityXL
duo-tour-holddrag-off   -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillTourState fresh -SillTour touch -Sill.holdThenDrag 0 --wait=6
duo-tour-holddrag-on    -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillTourState fresh -SillTour touch --wait=6
duo-stream-holddrag-on  -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat
